<title>USA: Schuller Q3 shr $0.21 vs $0.62 after gain.</title>
<headline>Schuller Q3 shr $0.21 vs $0.62 after gain.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schuller Net Income Analysis</p>
<p>			Three Months Ended September 30</p>
<p>	    (millions of dollars, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>							  1996	 1995</p>
<p>Net Income Applicable to</p>
<p> Common Stock - As Reported		    $33.9	$77.4</p>
<p>Adjustments (net of applicable tax):</p>
<p> Gain on Sale of Equity Investment			 (48.7)</p>
<p> Interest Expense on 9% Debentures			     .5</p>
<p> Profit Sharing Expense					   5.6</p>
<p> Income from Discontinued Operations		     (13.5)</p>
<p> Preference Stock Dividends				     6.2</p>
<p>Net Income - As Adjusted for</p>
<p> Nonrecurring Items				 33.9	 27.5</p>
<p>Earnings Per Common Share:</p>
<p> As reported*					 0.21	 0.62</p>
<p> As adjusted**					0.21	 0.17</p>
<p>*  Based upon 162.6 million and 125.4 million weighted average shares in the 1996 and 1995 periods, respectively.</p>
<p>**  Based upon net income as adjusted and 162.6 million weighted average shares.</p>
